<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of rain-affected four-day</p>
<p>English county championship cricket matches on Saturday:</p>
<p>At Derby: Derbyshire v Surrey match drawn. Surrey 267.</p>
<p>Derbyshire 158-3 (G.Khan 62 not out). Derbyshire 7 points Surrey</p>
<p>6.</p>
<p>At Hartlepool: Durham v Nottinghamshire match drawn.</p>
<p>Nottinghamshire 170 and 200-6 (R.Robinson 69). Durham 331.</p>
<p>Durham 10 points Notts 7.</p>
<p>At Bristol: Gloucestershire beat Hampshire by six wickets.</p>
<p>Hampshire 316 and 145 (A.Smith 6-45). Gloucestershire 403 and</p>
<p>59-4 (J.Renshaw 4-30). Gloucester 24 points Hampshire 6.</p>
<p>At Northampton: Northamptonshire v Somerset match drawn.</p>
<p>Northamptonshire 185 and 122-5. Somerset 290. Northants 7 points</p>
<p>Somerset 9.</p>
<p>At Worcester: Worcestershire v Leicestershire match drawn.</p>
<p>Worcestershire 257, Leicestershire 69 and 141-4 (N.Johnson 87</p>
<p>not out). Worcestershire 6 points Leicestershire 4.</p>
<p>At Headingley: Glamorgan v Yorkshire match drawn. Glamorgan</p>
<p>336 and 166-2 declared (H.Morris 96, S.James 52). Yorkshire</p>
<p>200-9 declared. Yorkshire 8 points Glamorgan 10.</p>
<p>At Lord's: Middlesex v Sussex match drawn. Middlesex 490-9</p>
<p>declared, Sussex 187 and 119-6 (J.Hewitt 4-24). Middlesex 11</p>
<p>points Sussex 5.</p>
</text>
